| Topic                         | Syntax / Example                  | Explanation                                                                                                                                     |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Python Program**            | `print("Hello World")`            | A Python program is a set of instructions that Python executes.                                                                                 |
| **Python File**               | `program.py`                      | Python source files normally use the `.py` extension.                                                                                           |
| **Statement**                 | `x = 10`                          | A statement is an instruction that Python executes.                                                                                             |
| **Expression**                | `10 + 20`                         | An expression produces a value.                                                                                                                 |
| **Print Output**              | `print("Hello")`                  | `print()` displays information on the screen.                                                                                                   |
| **Multiple Values in print**  | `print("Age:", 20)`               | `print()` can display multiple values separated by commas.                                                                                      |
| **String**                    | `"Hello"`                         | Text is written inside quotes.                                                                                                                  |
| **Single Quotes**             | `'Hello'`                         | Single quotes can be used for strings.                                                                                                          |
| **Double Quotes**             | `"Hello"`                         | Double quotes can also be used for strings.                                                                                                     |
| **Triple Quotes**             | `"""Hello"""`                     | Used mainly for multi-line strings and docstrings.                                                                                              |
| **Comment**                   | `# This is a comment`             | A comment is ignored by Python and is used to explain code. ([Python documentation][1])                                                         |
| **Multi-line Comment**        | `"""text"""`                      | Python has no dedicated multi-line comment syntax; triple-quoted strings are often used for documentation, though they are technically strings. |
| **Variable**                  | `name = "John"`                   | A variable is a name referring to a value/object.                                                                                               |
| **Variable Assignment**       | `x = 10`                          | `=` assigns a value to a variable.                                                                                                              |
| **Multiple Assignment**       | `a, b = 10, 20`                   | Multiple variables can be assigned in one statement.                                                                                            |
| **Same Value Assignment**     | `a = b = 10`                      | Multiple variables can refer to the same value.                                                                                                 |
| **Integer**                   | `x = 10`                          | Whole-number values such as `10`, `-5`, `100`.                                                                                                  |
| **Float**                     | `x = 10.5`                        | Decimal numbers such as `10.5`, `3.14`.                                                                                                         |
| **Complex**                   | `x = 2 + 3j`                      | Complex numbers have real and imaginary parts.                                                                                                  |
| **String Data**               | `name = "John"`                   | Stores text.                                                                                                                                    |
| **Boolean**                   | `is_valid = True`                 | Boolean values are `True` or `False`.                                                                                                           |
| **None**                      | `x = None`                        | Represents the absence of a value.                                                                                                              |
| **List**                      | `nums = [1, 2, 3]`                | An ordered, mutable collection.                                                                                                                 |
| **Tuple**                     | `nums = (1, 2, 3)`                | An ordered, generally immutable collection.                                                                                                     |
| **Set**                       | `nums = {1, 2, 3}`                | An unordered collection of unique elements.                                                                                                     |
| **Dictionary**                | `user = {"name": "John"}`         | Stores data as key-value pairs.                                                                                                                 |
| **`type()`**                  | `type(x)`                         | Tells you the type of an object.                                                                                                                |
| **Input**                     | `name = input("Name: ")`          | Gets input from the user. `input()` returns a string.                                                                                           |
| **Integer Input**             | `age = int(input("Age: "))`       | Converts user input to an integer.                                                                                                              |
| **Float Input**               | `price = float(input("Price: "))` | Converts user input to a float.                                                                                                                 |
| **Type Conversion**           | `int("10")`                       | Converts a compatible value to an integer.                                                                                                      |
| **String Conversion**         | `str(100)`                        | Converts a value to a string.                                                                                                                   |
| **Float Conversion**          | `float("10.5")`                   | Converts a compatible value to a float.                                                                                                         |
| **Arithmetic `+`**            | `10 + 5`                          | Addition.                                                                                                                                       |
| **Arithmetic `-`**            | `10 - 5`                          | Subtraction.                                                                                                                                    |
| **Arithmetic `*`**            | `10 * 5`                          | Multiplication.                                                                                                                                 |
| **Arithmetic `/`**            | `10 / 5`                          | Division; normally produces a float.                                                                                                            |
| **Floor Division `//`**       | `10 // 3`                         | Division rounded down to the floor.                                                                                                             |
| **Modulus `%`**               | `10 % 3`                          | Gives the remainder.                                                                                                                            |
| **Power `**`**                | `2 ** 3`                          | Raises a number to a power.                                                                                                                     |
| **Comparison `==`**           | `x == 10`                         | Checks equality.                                                                                                                                |
| **Comparison `!=`**           | `x != 10`                         | Checks inequality.                                                                                                                              |
| **Comparison `>`**            | `x > 10`                          | Greater than.                                                                                                                                   |
| **Comparison `<`**            | `x < 10`                          | Less than.                                                                                                                                      |
| **Comparison `>=`**           | `x >= 10`                         | Greater than or equal to.                                                                                                                       |
| **Comparison `<=`**           | `x <= 10`                         | Less than or equal to.                                                                                                                          |
| **Logical `and`**             | `age >= 18 and age <= 60`         | Both conditions must be true.                                                                                                                   |
| **Logical `or`**              | `x == 1 or x == 2`                | At least one condition must be true.                                                                                                            |
| **Logical `not`**             | `not is_valid`                    | Reverses a Boolean condition.                                                                                                                   |
| **Membership `in`**           | `"a" in "apple"`                  | Checks whether a value exists in a sequence.                                                                                                    |
| **Membership `not in`**       | `"z" not in "apple"`              | Checks whether a value does not exist.                                                                                                          |
| **Identity `is`**             | `x is None`                       | Checks object identity, not ordinary value equality.                                                                                            |
| **Identity `is not`**         | `x is not None`                   | Checks that two references are not the same object.                                                                                             |
| **Assignment `=`**            | `x = 10`                          | Assigns a value.                                                                                                                                |
| **Addition Assignment**       | `x += 5`                          | Equivalent to `x = x + 5`.                                                                                                                      |
| **Subtraction Assignment**    | `x -= 5`                          | Equivalent to `x = x - 5`.                                                                                                                      |
| **Multiplication Assignment** | `x *= 5`                          | Equivalent to `x = x * 5`.                                                                                                                      |
| **Division Assignment**       | `x /= 5`                          | Equivalent to `x = x / 5`.                                                                                                                      |
| **Floor Division Assignment** | `x //= 5`                         | Equivalent to `x = x // 5`.                                                                                                                     |
| **Modulus Assignment**        | `x %= 5`                          | Equivalent to `x = x % 5`.                                                                                                                      |
| **Power Assignment**          | `x **= 2`                         | Equivalent to `x = x ** 2`.                                                                                                                     |
| **Bitwise AND**               | `a & b`                           | Performs bitwise AND.                                                                                                                           |
| **Bitwise OR**                | `a \| b`                          | Performs bitwise OR.                                                                                                                            |
| **Bitwise XOR**               | `a ^ b`                           | Performs bitwise XOR.                                                                                                                           |
| **Left Shift**                | `a << 2`                          | Shifts bits to the left.                                                                                                                        |
| **Right Shift**               | `a >> 2`                          | Shifts bits to the right.                                                                                                                       |
| **Line Ending**               | `x = 10`<br>`y = 20`              | Usually, the end of a line ends a simple statement; Python does not require `;` at the end. ([Google Developers][2])                            |
| **Semicolon**                 | `x = 10; y = 20`                  | Multiple simple statements can be placed on one logical line, but this is generally less readable. ([GitHub][3])                                |
| **Indentation**               | `if x > 5:`<br>    `print(x)`     | Indentation defines code blocks in Python. ([GitHub][4])                                                                                        |
| **Standard Indentation**      | `    print(x)`                    | **4 spaces** are the usual recommended indentation style. ([Python Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)][5])                                            |
| **Colon `:`**                 | `if x > 5:`                       | Introduces the indented block following compound statements.                                                                                    |
| **Case Sensitive**            | `name` ≠ `Name`                   | Python treats uppercase and lowercase names as different. ([Google Developers][2])                                                              |
| **Identifier**                | `student_name`                    | A name used for variables, functions, classes, etc.                                                                                             |
| **Valid Identifier**          | `student_name`                    | Can contain letters, digits, and `_`, but cannot start with a digit.                                                                            |
| **Invalid Identifier**        | `2name`                           | An identifier cannot start with a number.                                                                                                       |
| **Underscore**                | `_name`                           | An underscore can be used at the beginning of an identifier.                                                                                    |
| **Snake Case**                | `student_name`                    | Common Python naming style for variables and functions.                                                                                         |
| **Keywords**                  | `if`, `for`, `while`, `class`     | Reserved words that have special meaning in Python.                                                                                             |
| **Import**                    | `import math`                     | Imports a module so its functionality can be used.                                                                                              |
| **From Import**               | `from math import sqrt`           | Imports a specific name from a module.                                                                                                          |
| **Alias**                     | `import numpy as np`              | Gives an imported module a shorter/local name.                                                                                                  |
| **Function Definition**       | `def add(a, b):`                  | Defines a function.                                                                                                                             |
| **Function Call**             | `add(10, 20)`                     | Executes/calls a function.                                                                                                                      |
| **`return`**                  | `return a + b`                    | Sends a value back from a function.                                                                                                             |
| **Block Structure**           | `if`, `for`, `def`, `class`       | Python uses indentation to group statements into blocks.                                                                                        |
| **Line Continuation**         | `total = (10 + 20 +`<br>    `30)` | Parentheses, brackets, and braces allow an expression to continue across lines.                                                                 |
| **String Concatenation**      | `"Hello " + "World"`              | Joins strings together.                                                                                                                         |
| **String Repetition**         | `"Hi " * 3`                       | Repeats a string.                                                                                                                               |
| **Indexing**                  | `"Python"[0]`                     | Accesses an element by position.                                                                                                                |
| **Slicing**                   | `"Python"[0:3]`                   | Extracts part of a sequence.                                                                                                                    |
| **F-string**                  | `f"Age: {age}"`                   | Convenient way to insert values into strings.                                                                                                   |
| **Escape Character**          | `"Hello\nWorld"`                  | `\n` represents a newline.                                                                                                                      |
| **Tab Escape**                | `"Hello\tWorld"`                  | `\t` represents a tab.                                                                                                                          |
| **Raw String**                | `r"C:\new\test"`                  | Treats backslashes mostly as literal characters.                                                                                                |
| **Blank Line**                | Empty line                        | Blank lines can improve readability and are generally ignored by Python's parser. ([Python documentation][6])                                   |
| **Code Block**                | `if x:`<br>    `print(x)`         | The indented statements belong to the `if` block.                                                                                               |
| **Readable Code**             | `student_name = "John"`           | Meaningful names and consistent formatting make code easier to understand.                                                                      |


